'## What a discovered mechanic actually does','',
'A preserved round32 modular descendant, `modular/0/familiar/mutation/g24/b39`, comes from random founder79 through12 mutation births. Its116-instruction genome has only four primitive nodes in the static recurrent output/halt dependency cone. Those implement:',
'','```text','C1(next) = positive neighbor signal from C6','C2(next) = C1 OR previous C2       # visible output','C6(next) = C1 OR previous C6       # persistent explored region','C7(next) = C1 OR previous C7       # halt signal','```','',
'The runtime’s initial goal pulse enters C1. The organism grows an accumulating goal-origin wave, advancing one edge everytwo ticks. When it reaches the source at distance d, it stops at2d+1 ticks and emits the entire goal-distance ball of radius d. This exact mask/timing prediction matches all168 emitted reachable development outputs. The result is a genuine generalizable exploration mechanic, but its raster includes explored branches. It does not retain a parent chain or extract one route. Other instructions still execute and cost work; finite budgets and disconnected behavior remain separate.','',
