'## Decision and next research direction','',
'The architectural change produced understandable, heritable exploration and modular reuse. It did not yet produce the crucial separation between exploring the maze and emitting only the selected route. The inspected effective programs remain tiny even inside much longer genomes; additional gene capacity alone has not translated into a multi-stage solver. More evolutionary time remains a live hypothesis, not a conclusion established by this pilot.','',
'Preserve these lineages and their complementary skills. The next useful bounded study is a mutation-accessibility comparison around the frozen wave and delayed-wave lineages: can generic mutations retain correct routing while reducing branch output on matched longer-prefix/cyclic cases, and do those improvements transfer to ordinary mazes? Include unchanged and matched random alternatives, freeze choices before fresh confirmation, and measure effective mechanism changes and losses. Do not install a backtrace, oracle cleanup or solver-specific module into a random-origin lineage. A subsequent60–90min continuation should be a documented new phase justified by those results, not an automatic rerun or a declaration that more time cannot help. Sexual recombination remains optional until demonstrated compatible complementary modules justify its cost.','',
